220-015-2433-6","volume":"339","author":"J Costa","year":"2015","unstructured":"Costa, J., Gir\u00e3o, P., Nat\u00e1rio, J., Silva, J.: On the global uniqueness for the Einstein\u2013Maxwell-scalar field system with a cosmological constant. Part 2: Structure of the solutions and stability of the Cauchy horizon. Commun. Math. Phys. 339, 903\u2013947 (2015). https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1007\/s00220-015-2433-6","journal-title":"Commun. Math. Phys."},{"key":"1454_CR18","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/s40818-017-0028-6","author":"J Costa","year":"2017","unstructured":"Costa, J., Gir\u00e3o, P., Nat\u00e1rio, J., Silva, J.: On the global uniqueness for the Einstein\u2013Maxwell-scalar field system with a cosmological constant. Part 3: Mass inflation and extendibility of the solutions. Ann. PDE (2017). https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1007\/s40818-017-0028-6","journal-title":"Ann. PDE"},{"key":"1454_CR19","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"289","DOI":"10.1007\/s00220-018-3122-z","volume":"361","author":"J Costa","year":"2018","unstructured":"Costa, J., Gir\u00e3o, P., Nat\u00e1rio, J., Silva, J.: On the occurrence of mass inflation for the Einstein\u2013Maxwell-scalar field system with a cosmological constant and an exponential Price law. Commun. Math. Phys. 361, 289\u2013341 (2018). https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1007\/s00220-018-3122-z","journal-title":"Commun. Math. Phys."},{"key":"1454_CR20","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1088\/1361-6382\/abb075","volume":"37","author":"JL Costa","year":"2020","unstructured":"Costa, J.L.: The formation of trapped surfaces in the gravitational collapse of spherically symmetric scalar fields with a positive cosmological constant. Class. Quantum Grav. 37, 195022 (2020). https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1088\/1361-6382\/abb075","journal-title":"Class. Quantum Grav."},{"key":"1454_CR21","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"40","DOI":"10.1007\/s13324-020-00380-5","volume":"10","author":"JL Costa","year":"2020","unstructured":"Costa, J.L., 